    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on May 11, **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the premier play with a score of 62.61. Despite facing a left-handed arm in Weathers, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong park factor and a favorable stolen base environment; Weathers\u2019 slow delivery provides the specific edge we covet to keep our SB ceiling high. **Heliot Ramos** is our next strongest start at 61.69, largely due to a soft matchup against Sasaki (5.30 xERA). While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.86) and **Kyle Tucker** (53.64) are facing a tougher challenge against McDonald, their elite profiles keep them in the starting lineup to ensure our core counting stats remain competitive despite the suboptimal opponent metrics.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's slate was the exclusion of **Josh Jung** (46.79), who narrowly missed the cut behind the more efficient profile of **Nolan Schanuel** (47.75). While **Josh Jung** provides solid middle-of-the-order production, the current projection suggests **Nolan Schanuel** is better positioned to contribute to our AVG floor. We are continuing to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, whose continued absence on the IL remains a significant drag on our outfield depth. Managers should also take note of **Andy Pages**, whose score dropped to 42.81\u2014the lowest in our active lineup\u2014due to the significant skill level of McDonald; he remains a start today, but with a narrow margin of error. Ensure all lineups are finalized, as we have no further weather alerts or late-scratch risks currently complicating the roster.",
